 -- Franco Conidi <fconidi@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 13:35:00 +0200

terminal-router (1.0.4) tirreno; urgency=medium

  * New command "terminal-router launch": logs a single self-contained tmux
    session instead of every terminal, with no edits to ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc
    or ~/.tmux.conf. Pipe-pane hooks are set on that one session only (no
    -g) and disappear with it, so other terminals — Terminator included —
    are unaffected.
  * install.sh: new "logdir-only" mode (used by "launch") that sets up
    ~/.claude-logs, pipe-logger.sh and the rotation cron without touching
    the shell rc file or ~/.tmux.conf.
  * menu: added "Launch a single logged session" entry.

 -- Franco Conidi <fconidi@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 13:15:00 +0200

terminal-router (1.0.3) tirreno; urgency=medium

  * postinst/postrm: stop rebuilding man, icon and desktop caches directly
    while APT holds its shutdown inhibitor. This avoids leaving the system
    unable to power off if an external cache updater stalls during package
    installation or removal.
  * terminal-router: report the packaged 1.0.3 version.

 -- Franco Conidi <fconidi@gmail.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 22:05:00 +0200

terminal-router (1.0.2) tirreno; urgency=medium

  * Menu placement, final: the entry now appears in the SysLinuxOS
    "Networking" and "SysLinuxOS Tools" menus, and nowhere else.
    - Networking comes from the X-SysLinuxOS-Networking category, which is
      also excluded from Accessories, Internet, System and Other, so the
      entry does not show up twice.
    - SysLinuxOS Tools includes entries by explicit filename, which no
      category can reach, so the package ships a menu drop-in in
      /etc/xdg/menus/applications-merged/ rather than patching
      /etc/xdg/menus/mate-applications.menu, a conffile owned by mate-menus.
  * postinst now mentions that MATE caches the menu and may need a panel
    restart.

 -- Franco Conidi <fconidi@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Sep 2026 21:41:00 +0200

terminal-router (1.0.1) tirreno; urgency=medium

  * Menu placement: add the X-SysLinuxOS-Networking category so the entry
    lands in the SysLinuxOS "Networking" menu, next to gtkterm and cutecom,
    instead of the generic "Internet" menu.
  * install: refuse to append a second block when an older, unmarked setup is
    detected, which would otherwise duplicate the tmux auto-start and define
    logpause/logresume twice.
  * status: report a detected unmarked legacy setup.
  * remove: warn that an unmarked legacy block cannot be removed automatically.
  * install: fix an abort on machines with no existing crontab, where
    "crontab -l" exits non-zero and set -e plus pipefail killed the installer
    before the hooks were written.

 -- Franco Conidi <fconidi@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Sep 2026 21:38:00 +0200

terminal-router (1.0.0) tirreno; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Packages the standalone claude-terminal-log installer as a SysLinuxOS
    menu entry with icon.
  * New terminal-router front-end: install, remove, status, tail, menu.
  * Adds a removal path (marked blocks deleted with backups, crontab entry
    dropped, optional log deletion) which the standalone script lacked.
  * tmux is now a package dependency, so the installer no longer prompts to
    install it.
  * Opt-in: nothing is logged until the user accepts the security notice.

 -- Franco Conidi <fconidi@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200
